  "summary" : "The service already has rate limiting (RateLimitService, RateLimitInterceptor, WebMvcConfig, RateLimitExceededException with a 429 handler) and syntactic URL validation (ValidUrl/HttpUrlValidator). Required changes: align the rate limit with the spec (default 60 requests/60s per IP, Retry-After header on 429, exclusion of any health endpoint); add SSRF protection that rejects loopback/private/link-local/unique-local/unspecified/localhost hosts, including hostnames that resolve to such addresses, with HTTP 400 and a reason, and no outbound call; ensure only http/https schemes are accepted; and introduce an external-check client with a 3s timeout and up to 2 retries (200ms fixed backoff) that surfaces failure as HTTP 503 with a JSON ErrorResponse (no stack trace) via GlobalExceptionHandler. UrlShortenerService must invoke the SSRF validation and external check before persisting, and must not persist anything on failure. Redirects must not be followed automatically (or each hop re-validated). Failures and rejections are logged at WARN without sensitive data. Automated tests are needed for each AC.",
